# The JARVIS subsystem is stored and checked out byte-for-byte.
#
# The repository root (N.E.K.O) normalises text to LF. JARVIS must not be touched by that: skill PROVENANCE.json files and the
# deployment sync compare SHA-256 hashes of these exact bytes, so a CRLF -> LF rewrite would break provenance and look like drift.
* -text
